summary:
- topic: Reconfiguration Timeline Delay
  text: The Board Chair announced a delay in the elementary school reconfiguration
    timeline to Fall 2027, citing community feedback and the need for a more thorough
    process. This decision aims to allow for sufficient public notice and proper development
    of the action plan.
- topic: Student & Staff Recognition
  text: Skillin Elementary Principal Bethany Connolly was recognized as the Maine
    Association of School Libraries Administrator of the Year for her exceptional
    support of the school library program. The Championship Boys Indoor SPHS Track
    Team was also celebrated for their state championship season, with Coach Cahill
    receiving the Portland Press Herald Coach of the Year award.
- topic: FY26-27 Budget Update
  text: The Director of Finance provided a budget update, including a location-based
    analysis of school costs and potential tax increase impacts. She highlighted the
    financial implications of a school closure and emphasized the need for careful
    planning for the upcoming fiscal year due to many unknowns.
- topic: Special Education Staffing & Challenges
  text: The Director of Instructional Support presented an update on special education,
    detailing the embedded Occupational Therapy (OT) model and ongoing challenges
    with EdTech staffing. Strategies for recruitment, training, and potential partnerships
    with outside agencies were discussed to address these staffing needs.
- topic: Community Feedback on Budget & Reconfiguration
  text: Public comment periods featured extensive feedback from parents, teachers,
    and community members, largely expressing gratitude for the reconfiguration delay
    but also concern over budget cuts and their impact on staff and programs. Speakers
    emphasized the need for transparency, data-driven decisions, and community engagement
    in shaping the district's vision.
- topic: Financial Requests to City Council
  text: The Board voted to formally request the City Council to offset $360,000 in
    costs for shared municipal services, including School Resource Officers (SROs)
    and snow removal. Additionally, the Board requested a 1% tax increase to specifically
    seed the district's contingency fund, with any funds from the municipal services
    offset also directed to contingency.
- topic: Vice Chair Election
  text: Tyler Smith was unanimously elected as the new Vice Chair of the School Board,
    following the resignation of Adrian Dowling. The Chair expressed confidence in
    his commitment and thoughtful approach to the role.
